tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#table-stripes-and-column-resize","content":"Table stripes and column resize"},"32":{"id":"/docs/changelog-30","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"Table"},"33":{"id":"/docs/changelog-31","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#icons","content":"Icons"},"34":{"id":"/docs/changelog-32","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#data-tables","content":"Data tables"},"35":{"id":"/docs/changelog-33","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#september-2026","content":"September 2026"},"36":{"id":"/docs/changelog-34","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#registry-on-vittaldesign","content":"Registry on vittal.design"},"37":{"id":"/docs/changelog-35","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#install","content":"Install"},"38":{"id":"/docs/changelog-36","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#components-9","content":"Components"},"39":{"id":"/docs/changelog-37","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#blocks","content":"Blocks"},"40":{"id":"/docs/changelog-38","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#tokens","content":"Tokens"},"41":{"id":"/docs/changelog-39","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#platform","content":"Platform"},"42":{"id":"/docs/changelog-40","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"This page tracks the registry-backed design system on vittal.design: components, blocks, icons, and tokens. It does not track the legacy @fed/vital-design npm package."},"43":{"id":"/docs/changelog-41","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"That package is built from src/ and stays available for existing apps. New work ships through the registry. If you still import from the package, see the Migration Guide."},"44":{"id":"/docs/changelog-42","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"Entries are grouped by the month they shipped, newest first. We only record changes that affect how you install or use the registry — new components, breaking usage, tokens, and install steps. Documentation-only updates, such as new examples, are not listed."},"45":{"id":"/docs/changelog-43","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"Sidebar: new optional props for sidebars that live inside another app's page or share a page with a second sidebar:"},"46":{"id":"/docs/changelog-44","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"SidebarProvider cookieName writes the open state under another cookie name; cookieName={null} writes no cookie."},"47":{"id":"/docs/changelog-45","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"SidebarProvider isMobile replaces the built-in 768px check. isMobile={false} never switches to the mobile Sheet."},"48":{"id":"/docs/changelog-46","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"SidebarTrigger takes children to replace its icon and render to use another element, such as render={<Button variant=\"ghost\" size=\"icon-md\" />}. A rendered element keeps its own look. Calling event.preventDefault() in onClick stops the toggle."},"49":{"id":"/docs/changelog-47","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"Sidebar takes render to change its root element, such as <aside /> or <nav />. It is ignored on mobile, where the panel is a Sheet."},"50":{"id":"/docs/changelog-48","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"SidebarMenuButton no longer throws outside a SidebarProvider; it renders as expanded, without its tooltip."},"51":{"id":"/docs/changelog-49","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components","content":"Leaving the new props out keeps the current behavior. Reinstall sidebar to pick this up."},"52":{"id":"/docs/changelog-50","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"New icon items, all drawn by the design team in the 20×20 frame:"},"53":{"id":"/docs/changelog-51","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Status: icon-circle-check, icon-circle-check-solid, icon-circle-xmark, icon-circle-xmark-solid, icon-circle-info, icon-circle-info-solid, icon-circle-exclamation-solid, icon-circle-minus-solid, icon-circle-question, icon-exclamation-solid, icon-circle-dashed, icon-circle-dot."},"54":{"id":"/docs/changelog-52","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Files and arrows: icon-file-lines, icon-file-arrow-up-solid, icon-arrow-right-long, icon-arrow-up-right-from-square, icon-arrow-up-right-from-square-solid."},"55":{"id":"/docs/changelog-53","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Other: icon-clock-solid, icon-ellipsis-vertical, icon-grip-dots-vertical."},"56":{"id":"/docs/changelog-54","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"InfoIcon is renamed CircleInfoIcon (@vital-design/icon-circle-info) to match the design list, and now uses the design artwork. The old name and registry item still work but are deprecated; InfoIcon re-exports CircleInfoIcon. Switch to the new name."},"57":{"id":"/docs/changelog-55","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Updated artwork:"},"58":{"id":"/docs/changelog-56","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"ClockIcon uses the redrawn design artwork; the hand is redrawn."},"59":{"id":"/docs/changelog-57","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"ClearIcon uses the redrawn design artwork; the circle is centred in the frame (it sat 0.25px high) and the × is larger."},"60":{"id":"/docs/changelog-58","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"CalendarDaysIcon is about 0.25px larger on each side, matching the design file."},"61":{"id":"/docs/changelog-59","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"CircleUserIcon, SidebarIcon, and ThumbtackSolidIcon look the same but are now drawn with strokes, so the strokeWidth prop changes their line weight like the other icons."},"62":{"id":"/docs/changelog-60","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Component changes:"},"63":{"id":"/docs/changelog-61","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"data-table: the drag handle in the column-visibility popover is now a 20px GripDotsVerticalIcon instead of six drawn dots."},"64":{"id":"/docs/changelog-62","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"sidebar-cloud-04: the Support item uses CircleInfoIcon, and the external-link mark uses ArrowUpRightFromSquareIcon."},"65":{"id":"/docs/changelog-63","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Temporary artwork. These icons still use placeholder artwork until the design team confirms the final version. Only the SVG will change:"},"66":{"id":"/docs/changelog-64","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Font Awesome Pro in the design file, so the previous Vittal artwork is used instead: MagnifyingGlassIcon, PlusIcon, SpinnerIcon, ShieldCheckIcon, SquareArrowOutUpRightIcon."},"67":{"id":"/docs/changelog-65","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Font Awesome Free shapes not yet redrawn: FlagIcon, UserIcon."},"68":{"id":"/docs/changelog-66","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Not in the design file yet: PanelLeftIcon."},"69":{"id":"/docs/changelog-67","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#status-file-and-arrow-icons-from-the-design-list","content":"Drawn by design but not yet confirmed: XmarkIcon, EyeIcon."},"70":{"id":"/docs/changelog-68","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#tree-select","content":"Tree Select: a new block for searchable hierarchical path pickers, built from Command and Popover. Pass a flat item list; selecting a leaf returns its value and the path from the top level. It replaces the Hierarchical Picker example that was on the Command page."},"71":{"id":"/docs/changelog-69","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-1","content":"Tooltip, Select, Combobox, Autocomplete, Dropdown Menu: TooltipContent, SelectContent, ComboboxContent, AutocompleteContent, DropdownMenuContent, and DropdownMenuSubContent now take the same portal and positioning props as PopoverContent:"},"72":{"id":"/docs/changelog-70","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-1","content":"portalContainer renders the popup inside another node, such as a CSS-scoped root, instead of document.body."},"73":{"id":"/docs/changelog-71","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-1","content":"anchor positions the popup against an element other than the trigger."},"74":{"id":"/docs/changelog-72","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-1","content":"collisionBoundary, collisionPadding, collisionAvoidance, positionMethod, sticky, arrowPadding, and disableAnchorTracking go to the positioner."},"75":{"id":"/docs/changelog-73","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-1","content":"keepMounted goes to the portal. SelectContent doesn't have it, because Base UI's Select portal doesn't accept it."},"76":{"id":"/docs/changelog-74","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-1","content":"All are optional; leaving them out keeps the current behavior. DropdownMenuSubContent used to pass anchor to the popup element; it now positions the submenu. Reinstall tooltip, select, combobox, autocomplete, or dropdown-menu to pick this up."},"77":{"id":"/docs/changelog-75","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-2","content":"Popover: PopoverContent accepts anchor, so a popover can be positioned against an element other than its trigger, or opened with no trigger at all. It also accepts portalContainer, like DropdownMenuContent, to render the popup inside a scoped root instead of document.body. If you patched these props into your copy, you can drop the patch. See Custom Anchor and Portal Container."},"78":{"id":"/docs/changelog-76","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-2","content":"PopoverContent also passes collisionBoundary, collisionPadding, collisionAvoidance, positionMethod, sticky, arrowPadding, and disableAnchorTracking to the positioner, and keepMounted to the portal. All are optional; leaving them out keeps the current behavior. Reinstall popover to pick this up."},"79":{"id":"/docs/changelog-77","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-3","content":"Table of Contents: now a registry item. Install it with npx shadcn@latest add @vital-design/table-of-contents. It's a compact rail of section ticks that expands into the full list of headings on hover or keyboard focus. See Table of Contents."},"80":{"id":"/docs/changelog-78","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Reinstall the theme to pick up dark colors:"},"81":{"id":"/docs/changelog-79","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Light values stay on :root. The same custom properties change when an ancestor has class=\"dark\". prefers-color-scheme does not switch them. See Colors → Dark mode."},"82":{"id":"/docs/changelog-80","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Primitive scales, and semantic aliases that point at those scales, have dark values. background, card, and popover are #232327, and input is #444447. The .dark ancestor uses that paper and the dark foreground. border and border-overlap alias scales, so they follow them: white at 0.08 and #444447."},"83":{"id":"/docs/changelog-81","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Scale classes switch too. Under .dark, a scale class such as bg-grayscale-50 or text-primary-500 resolves to that scale's dark value. This is part of the theme's contract, so a scale class in your own code changes with the mode. Fixed Tailwind colors and arbitrary values do not: bg-white stays white and is reserved for marks such as switch thumbs, and text-white stays white."},"84":{"id":"/docs/changelog-82","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Components used to paint their paper with bg-white, which stays white in dark mode. They now use bg-background, and some also fix text that was hard to read on dark paper. Reinstall the theme and the items you use:"},"85":{"id":"/docs/changelog-83","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"The theme also adds a dark: variant that matches inside a .dark ancestor."},"86":{"id":"/docs/changelog-84","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Known limitations, still waiting on design:"},"87":{"id":"/docs/changelog-85","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"warning-foreground follows the grayscale ink, so it turns white under .dark, and text on warning fills loses contrast. The other white foregrounds, such as primary-foreground, stay white."},"88":{"id":"/docs/changelog-86","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Avatar and Tag palettes, shadows, and gradients have no dark values."},"89":{"id":"/docs/changelog-87","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"Solid buttons keep white text."},"90":{"id":"/docs/changelog-88","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"The frosted backdrop in the sidebar-cloud blocks stays light, so their menu text is hard to read in dark mode."},"91":{"id":"/docs/changelog-89","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#dark-color-tokens","content":"The info Tooltip and info Toast keep their current dark backgrounds."},"92":{"id":"/docs/changelog-90","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-4","content":"SplitButton: splitRender turns the chevron into a menu trigger, so <SplitButton splitRender={<DropdownMenuTrigger />}> inside a DropdownMenu opens, positions, and closes the menu without your own state or anchor. open is now optional, and splitLabel sets the chevron's accessible name. Existing open + splitOnClick code keeps working. See SplitButton. Reinstall split-button to pick this up."},"93":{"id":"/docs/changelog-91","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-5","content":"Tag: no longer renders role=\"option\" or aria-selected. A clickable Tag with selected now sets aria-pressed on its button. If your tests find Tags with getByRole('option'), query by text or data-slot=\"tag\" instead. Reinstall tag to pick this up."},"94":{"id":"/docs/changelog-92","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-5","content":"Data Table: the tags editor shows each choice as a Tag, the same pill as the cell, instead of plain text. Reinstall data-table to pick this up."},"95":{"id":"/docs/changelog-93","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#pagination","content":"Pagination: added composable page links, first/last and previous/next controls, disabled states, and an ellipsis that opens a menu of the hidden pages. Use anchors for navigation or compose native buttons with render for in-place updates. Installing @vital-design/pagination also installs the angle icons it uses."},"96":{"id":"/docs/changelog-94","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#pagination","content":"Table Pagination: a single-row table footer with page controls, a page jump, rows per page, and the current range. Narrow rows hide the jump field and the page-size select."},"97":{"id":"/docs/changelog-95","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-6","content":"Breadcrumb: now available from the registry as breadcrumb. See Breadcrumb."},"98":{"id":"/docs/changelog-96","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Breaking: icon names now match the design team's icon list. The old registry items are removed."},"99":{"id":"/docs/changelog-97","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Old item"},"100":{"id":"/docs/changelog-98","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"New item"},"101":{"id":"/docs/changelog-99","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-chevron-left"},"102":{"id":"/docs/changelog-100","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-angle-left"},"103":{"id":"/docs/changelog-101","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-chevron-right"},"104":{"id":"/docs/changelog-102","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-angle-right"},"105":{"id":"/docs/changelog-103","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-chevron-double-left"},"106":{"id":"/docs/changelog-104","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-angles-left"},"107":{"id":"/docs/changelog-105","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-chevron-double-right"},"108":{"id":"/docs/changelog-106","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-angles-right"},"109":{"id":"/docs/changelog-107","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-chevron-down"},"110":{"id":"/docs/changelog-108","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-angle-down"},"111":{"id":"/docs/changelog-109","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-chevron-up"},"112":{"id":"/docs/changelog-110","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-angle-up"},"113":{"id":"/docs/changelog-111","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-close"},"114":{"id":"/docs/changelog-112","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-xmark"},"115":{"id":"/docs/changelog-113","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-disabled"},"116":{"id":"/docs/changelog-114","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-ban"},"117":{"id":"/docs/changelog-115","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-calendar"},"118":{"id":"/docs/changelog-116","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-calendar-days"},"119":{"id":"/docs/changelog-117","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-search"},"120":{"id":"/docs/changelog-118","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"@vital-design/icon-magnifying-glass"},"121":{"id":"/docs/changelog-119","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Update imports to the new component names: AngleLeftIcon, AngleRightIcon, AnglesLeftIcon, AnglesRightIcon, AngleDownIcon, AngleUpIcon, XmarkIcon, BanIcon, CalendarDaysIcon, MagnifyingGlassIcon. Reinstall the components you use; every component that depended on a renamed item now depends on the new one."},"122":{"id":"/docs/changelog-120","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"The carets take the Solid suffix, because a plain name means the Regular style: CaretDownIcon and CaretUpIcon are now CaretDownSolidIcon and CaretUpSolidIcon (@vital-design/icon-caret-down-solid, @vital-design/icon-caret-up-solid). The old names and registry items still work but are deprecated; CaretDownIcon re-exports CaretDownSolidIcon. Switch to the new names."},"123":{"id":"/docs/changelog-121","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"New icon items: icon-angle-down-solid, icon-angle-up-solid, icon-angle-left-solid, icon-angle-right-solid, icon-angle-left-to-line, icon-angle-right-to-line, icon-check-solid, icon-minus-solid, icon-bars, icon-circle-user, icon-home, icon-inbox, icon-life-ring, icon-planet-ringed, icon-sidebar, icon-thumbtack, icon-thumbtack-solid, icon-bell-slash, icon-caret-left-solid, icon-caret-right-solid, icon-note, icon-placeholder, icon-placeholder-solid. PlaceholderIcon is the design's *icons: a stand-in for a slot that takes any icon. See Icons → Regular and Solid."},"124":{"id":"/docs/changelog-122","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Every icon now uses a 20×20 frame with padding, so a size-* class sets the frame, not the glyph. Components size icons to the Figma frame: icons inside Button (data-icon) are 18px (md, icon-md) and 20px (lg, icon-lg) with no margin, and Sidebar menu icons are 20px. If you set your own icon sizes, check them against the new frames."},"125":{"id":"/docs/changelog-123","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Component changes that follow the design list:"},"126":{"id":"/docs/changelog-124","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"checkbox uses CheckSolidIcon and MinusSolidIcon."},"127":{"id":"/docs/changelog-125","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"number-input steppers use CaretUpSolidIcon and CaretDownSolidIcon."},"128":{"id":"/docs/changelog-126","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"split-button uses the regular angle on white themes and the solid angle on coloured themes."},"129":{"id":"/docs/changelog-127","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"The angle, angles, and angle-to-line icons use the redrawn design artwork, so the glyph is 10px tall in the 20px frame instead of 8.3px. This shows in calendar and split-button."},"130":{"id":"/docs/changelog-128","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"EllipsisIcon no longer has a built-in 0.55 fill opacity; it takes the text color like every other icon. In breadcrumb the collapsed ellipsis is now grayscale-500, the same as the other inactive items. If you added [fill-opacity:1] to undo it, remove it."},"131":{"id":"/docs/changelog-129","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"data-table group rows use a 20px CaretDownSolidIcon (rotated when collapsed), and the popover option check uses CheckSolidIcon like checkbox. The selection bar's close icon is 20px and the add-row plus is 18px."},"132":{"id":"/docs/changelog-130","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Temporary artwork. These icons keep their names and sizes, but the artwork is a placeholder until the design team draws the final version. Only the SVG will change:"},"133":{"id":"/docs/changelog-131","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Font Awesome Pro in the design file, so the previous Vittal artwork is used instead: MagnifyingGlassIcon, PlusIcon, SpinnerIcon, ShieldCheckIcon, SquareArrowOutUpRightIcon."},"134":{"id":"/docs/changelog-132","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Font Awesome Free shapes not yet redrawn: ClockIcon, FlagIcon, UserIcon, EllipsisIcon."},"135":{"id":"/docs/changelog-133","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Not in the design file yet: InfoIcon, ClearIcon, PanelLeftIcon."},"136":{"id":"/docs/changelog-134","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons-use-the-design-names-and-2020-frames","content":"Drawn by design but not yet confirmed: XmarkIcon, AngleLeftIcon, AngleRightIcon (and their Solid versions), AnglesLeftIcon, AnglesRightIcon, CircleUserIcon, ThumbtackSolidIcon."},"137":{"id":"/docs/changelog-135","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#border-tokens","content":"--border is now the 0.08 hairline (grayscale-opacity-200), the line Figma uses for dividers. It was a solid #DEDEE2. A new --border-overlap token keeps the solid #DEDEE2 for edges that stack or cross, where a translucent line would darken. Use it with border-border-overlap."},"138":{"id":"/docs/changelog-136","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#border-tokens","content":"The theme also sets a default border color, so a bare border, border-t, or border-b draws the --border hairline. Before, Tailwind v4 drew it in the text color."},"139":{"id":"/docs/changelog-137","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#border-tokens","content":"Avatar, AvatarGroupCount, and the group rails in the Data Table block move to --border-overlap, so they look the same as before. The Dialog footer divider and any border-border you use for dividers get lighter. A FieldLabel that wraps a Field (the choice-card layout) draws its outline with a bare border, so it also goes from the text color to the hairline. Reinstall the theme and these items:"},"140":{"id":"/docs/changelog-138","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#data-table-block","content":"Breaking. The three data table blocks are replaced by one generic block, @vital-design/data-table. You pass it your own data and columns; it groups rows by any field, up to two levels, with a 新增 row per group. It also has search, sorting, resizable and reorderable columns, row selection with a floating action bar, and inline and popover cell editing. The checkbox and actions columns stay pinned and cast a shadow while other columns scroll under them. A review-task example shows how to wire it up. The block uses the new @vital-design/icon-gear."},"141":{"id":"/docs/changelog-139","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#data-table-block","content":"These ids are retired and leave the registry: @vital-design/data-table-group-01 (candidate tree), @vital-design/data-table-group-02 (ESG emission tree), and @vital-design/data-table-group-04 (editable cells). Copies you already installed keep working, since a block is your own code. To move over, install the new block and port your columns and rows; grouping by a field replaces the fixed tree rows. Not carried over yet: a row count in group headers, more than one left-pinned column, and columnResizeMode=\"onEnd\"."},"142":{"id":"/docs/changelog-140","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#data-table-block","content":"See Data Table."},"143":{"id":"/docs/changelog-141","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-7","content":"Dialog: the popup's max height now follows the viewport it sits in (max-h-full) instead of calc(100vh-2rem). On mobile browsers, 100vh is taller than the visible area while the address bar shows, so a tall dialog ran under the toolbar and lost its bottom spacing. It now keeps the viewport's 1rem padding and scrolls inside. If you added your own max-h-[calc(100dvh-…)] to work around this, you can drop it. Reinstall dialog to pick this up."},"144":{"id":"/docs/changelog-142","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-7","content":"Sheet: top and bottom sheets cap at 80dvh instead of 80vh, to match the h-dvh that left and right sheets already use. Reinstall sheet to pick this up."},"145":{"id":"/docs/changelog-143","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#react-19","content":"The registry and the docs site are developed and tested on React 19. New projects should use React 19. See Installation."},"146":{"id":"/docs/changelog-144","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#components-8","content":"Button: added LinkButton, a link styled as a button. It shares Button's variants, themes, and sizes, renders <a> (or a router link via render), and keeps link semantics. Use it instead of <Button nativeButton={false} render={<a />}>, which reports links as buttons. See Button → Link."},"147":{"id":"/docs/changelog-145","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"Table can stripe body rows. striped paints even rows. striped=\"odd\" paints the other rows. Set --table-stripe and --table-row-hover on the table to change the colors."},"148":{"id":"/docs/changelog-146","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"Reinstall the table to pick this up:"},"149":{"id":"/docs/changelog-147","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"Breaking: hover, expanded, and selected row backgrounds no longer use bg-grayscale-opacity-100. They read --table-row-hover. With striped left off, that variable still falls back to --grayscale-opacity-100, so the default look stays the same."},"150":{"id":"/docs/changelog-148","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"hover:bg-grayscale-opacity-100 → hover:bg-[var(--table-row-hover,var(--grayscale-opacity-100))]"},"151":{"id":"/docs/changelog-149","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"data-[state=selected]:bg-grayscale-opacity-100 → data-[state=selected]:bg-[var(--table-row-hover,var(--grayscale-opacity-100))]"},"152":{"id":"/docs/changelog-150","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#table","content":"TableHead is now position: relative. An absolutely positioned child lines up with the header cell. If one of yours was lined up with an ancestor outside the cell, point it at the cell instead."},"153":{"id":"/docs/changelog-151","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#icons","content":"Caret up and caret down are new registry icons. See Icons."},"154":{"id":"/docs/changelog-152","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#data-tables","content":"Data Table group 01 and group 02 can resize columns. Drag the header edge. columnResizeMode defaults to onChange. Use onEnd on a wide table with many pinned columns so the columns stay put until you release."},"155":{"id":"/docs/changelog-153","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#data-tables","content":"Reinstall both blocks. Group 02 also swaps its sort icon from chevron up to the caret pair, and drops @vital-design/icon-chevron-up. @vital-design/icon-chevron-down stays for the row rail. The sort label truncates so the caret stays visible when a column gets narrow."},"156":{"id":"/docs/changelog-154","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#registry-on-vittaldesign","content":"The documentation site and the shadcn-compatible registry now publish together at vittal.design. This entry is a snapshot of what is available today. Later entries will list only what changed."},"157":{"id":"/docs/changelog-155","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/