low."},"4091":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-23","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#status","content":"type accepts success, warning, error, info, or loading.\nThe toast applies the matching colour but does not pick an icon —\nicons are opt-in via data.icon. The loading status swaps the\nclose X for a cancel button when data.cancelProps is supplied."},"4092":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-24","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#position","content":"ToastProvider accepts a position prop with six anchors:\ntop-left, top-center, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-center,\nbottom-right. One provider serves one position — toasts dispatched\nthrough its manager render at that anchor."},"4093":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-25","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#multiple-positions-two-channels","content":"To send some toasts to one corner and others to a different corner,\ncreate a second manager with createToastManager and nest a second\nToastProvider for it. Each provider/manager pair is a separate\nchannel — pick whichever you want at the call site."},"4094":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-26","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#variants","content":"The solid variant (default) fills the toast with the status colour\non a white-on-coloured layout. The subtle variant flips to a white\nsurface with a tinted icon — matches the \"notification\" pattern in the\ndesign system."},"4095":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-27","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#loading","content":"For long-running operations, dispatch a toast with type: 'loading'\nand timeout: 0. Give it a data.cancelProps button, which replaces\nthe close X, so the user can cancel the operation, then update the\ntoast on completion."},"4096":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-28","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#with-icon","content":"Pass any icon node through data.icon; the renderer drops it into\nthe icon slot before the title."},"4097":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-29","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#with-description","content":"Add a second line of context with description."},"4098":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-30","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#with-action","content":"actionProps is forwarded to the action button. Use it for an \"Undo\"\nor other recovery affordance."},"4099":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-31","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#promise","content":"promise swaps a single toast through loading, success, and error\nstates based on a promise."},"4100":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-32","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#stacking","content":"Toasts in one viewport stack. Hover or focus the stack to expand it.\nWhen more than limit toasts (default 3) are open, the oldest one is\nremoved."},"4101":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-33","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#anchored-toasts","content":"For tooltip-style feedback anchored to a specific element (e.g.,\n\"Copied!\" near a button), use anchoredToastManager and wrap with\nAnchoredToastProvider. Pass positionerProps.anchor per call."},"4102":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-34","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#toastprovider","content":"Prop"},"4103":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-35","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#toastprovider","content":"Type"},"4104":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-36","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[